    "text": "6 hours ago LYNCHBURG, Tenn. — By 8 a.m. Friday, the oil will be heating in two big cookers set up outside Lynchburg First Methodist Church. Once it reaches 350 degrees, the women of the Lynchburg Ladies of Faith will brush the loose flour off roughly 500 frozen pies and lower them in — nine or 10 at a time. Each batch will take around four minutes. Read full article",
